From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Axel Garcia K." <git@axelgk.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:33:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] loader: move the directory buffer off the stack

Keep the 4 KiB ISO directory scratch space out of the constrained userspace stack.

Evidence: this is the previously reviewed frontend patch qpsx-static-load-buffer.patch, applied in its established build order on upstream 368310a.

Risk: limited to the paths recorded in that patch. Reverting this commit restores the preceding independently buildable checkpoint.
---
 src/misc.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/misc.cpp b/src/misc.cpp
index e48d2c2ac2cf299c6e43de9516a09373e945f26f..ce469289e0aa074a804c4fb8bb2683b9c87dda52 100644
--- a/src/misc.cpp
+++ b/src/misc.cpp
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@ int LoadCdrom() {
 	EXE_HEADER tmpHead;
 	struct iso_directory_record *dir;
 	u8 time[4], *buf;
-	u8 mdir[4096];
+	static u8 mdir[4096];
 	char exename[256];
 
 	// not the best place to do it, but since BIOS boot logo killer
